WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:36.820
Regarding Jamaican as an obstacle
to his advancement and independence...

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.500
...Yazan devised a plan to get rid of him
during the battle against the Argama.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.800
Although Yazan achieved his objective
through this plan...

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.740
...he realized that Scirocco wasn't likely
to overlook what actually happened.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:54.790
Rendezvous with Char

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.520
Fa! What's keeping you?!

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.130
Can't I at least
comb my hair first?

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.030
This upcoming battle is going
to be a tough one.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.200
From what I'm seeing,
you've failed as a pilot!

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.360
You don't suddenly have to
take care of me, you know.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.100
What the...?!

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.840
I'll go right away...

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.880
...so will you take that
annoying face out of here?!

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.950
All right.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.050
Fa! Emotionally excited! Excited!

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.610
I know that much!

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.880
Hi, Kamille! What's wrong?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:36.980
Nothing!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.230
Recreation's fine, but a worried look on a
young man's face is not necessarily healthy.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.860
It's only recreation!

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.830
Spit it out.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.530
Lieutenant Quattro's returning.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.240
We can't have him worry unnecessarily
about your affairs!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:59.140
Every time I talk with Fa, we end up
in a fight. I wonder why.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.340
That's what's bothering me.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.740
Well, you know...!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.880
Those are worries you can only experience
while still young.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.250
Worry, and learn.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.720
- Bye!
- Thanks for nothing!

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.760
The Alexandria's fleet
that left A Baoa Qu...

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:20.930
...is expected to arrive at Earth's
geostationary orbit about when we do...

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:21.930
...or sooner.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.640
<i>Can't we take a detour and</i>
<i>camouflage our true objectives?</i>

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.870
If we did that,
the shuttle Lieutenant Quattro is on...

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.440
...would have to wait along the
geostationary orbit longer than necessary.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.510
The fact we entered enemy territory
to receive laser communication...

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.250
...is now working against us.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.650
<i>We'll have to force our way</i>
<i>through, Captain Bright.</i>

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.880
I got delayed.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.790
Status of the mobile suit team?

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.290
I suggest we separate the Zeta
and the Methuss in our mission.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.030
Why's that?

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.190
- It has to do with the pilots.
- The pilots?

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.770
<i>Oh, Ensign Reccoa's</i>
<i>gone to Granada, right?</i>

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.770
Yes.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.810
And so Kamille and Fa would...!

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.440
The recreation topic again?

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.310
Well...!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.640
I'm just not suited
to be Kamille's father figure.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.380
Haven't the ship's internal
circuits been checked yet?!

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.390
We'll get right on it, sir.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.330
How do you expect us to sink
the Argama with you guys taking forever?!

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.200
All because I left this ship to Jamaican...

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.460
...the bridge gets destroyed.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.700
If it weren't for these repairs,
we would've caught up to the Argama!

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.700
Captain.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.000
Oh, thanks for coming.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.540
Is it okay for us to sortie
before repairs are complete?

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.150
Mouar!

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.210
Captain Gady called me here as well.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.310
Is that so?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.750
Because I also feel it's about time we
displayed the Alexandria's true potential.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.820
However, Yazan didn't
have to be called in.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.250
It's Scirocco.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.490
I understand he also has ties
with the leaders of the Gate of Zedan.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.030
Gate of Zedan?

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.160
Oh, right, A Baoa Qu.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.270
<i>Lieutenant Jerid!</i>

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.300
<i>I have an urgent call</i>
<i>from the mobile suit deck!</i>

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.340
What could it be?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:08.470
What is it?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.340
What did you say?
Okay, I'll be right there.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.840
What's wrong?

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.780
It's Yazan.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:15.370
Please excuse me.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.390
He says he's throwing out the Hizacks
no matter what.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.290
Damn Yazan!

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:27.920
What's the big idea?!

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:29.520
Jerid!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.760
Please stop it, Squadron Leader Yazan!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.770
<i>I can no longer bear the idea of trying</i>
<i>to fight with these pieces of junk!</i>

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:36.500
Lieutenant Jerid!

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:37.830
<i>Out of my way!</i>

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.500
Come out of the cockpit!

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.560
<i>Well, if it isn't the loser</i>
<i>who should be dead.</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.040
If you don't listen to me...

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.440
...I'll throw you in jail for treason!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.870
Would you stop the whining?

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.410
What's the big idea?!

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.880
I just don't want any outdated toys...

00:05:54.950 --> 00:06:00.090
...incomplete battle dolls like her
on any ship I'm on!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.760
Are you calling me a battle doll?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:03.990
Well, that's what you are.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.230
Yazan!

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.300
Jerid!

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.500
If you have any complaints, express them
after defeating the Zeta Gundam!

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.430
I'll listen to you then!

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:15.930
- I'll take those words seriously.
- As a man, I mean every word I say!

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:20.770
- Damn you!
- Jerid!

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.910
I suggest that you and that Cyber-Newtype...

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.950
...try to have a good time together.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.960
Aren't you going to ask
why I came to the Alexandria?

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.660
The truth is...

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.320
...Scirocco asked me to join him
on the Jupitris.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.800
I don't care about your circumstances.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.400
By eliminating the challenges you face,
such circumstances can be altered.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.470
Jerid!

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:55.350
I was delighted that Captain Gady
invited me to this ship.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.010
Because I knew you were on board.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.020
Mouar.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.480
Jerid, Scirocco is a
very unpredictable man.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.220
- You mustn't...!
- I understand.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:10.160
Don't say another word.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:22.980
Jerid!

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.830
I'm borrowing the Hizack
Yazan was toying with!

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.470
For what?

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.240
The Mega-Launcher is ready to use, right?

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.910
Are you serious?

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.390
That Hizack accompanies
Sarah's machine...

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.910
...merely as an energy tank
for the launcher she uses.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.050
We don't even know if you
could return safely.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.430
I came to be with you all the way.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.360
I won't die...

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.090
...because you'll be there to protect me.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.210
Okay.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.970
Course confirmed!
Synchronize clocks!

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.110
Be prepared for a lot more
than retrieving the shuttle!

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:07.520
Now that the main forces
have joined with the Titans...

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.560
...the enemy could come at us
from anywhere.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.660
Be prepared for
anti-air missile attacks!

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:15.690
Captain!

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.460
What is it?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.560
Please don't talk with your mouth full!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.120
All units!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.330
<i>Observe our surroundings</i>
<i>as if your life depended on it!</i>

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.560
Oh, boy!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.640
Kamille!

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.640
- Go to the rear of the Argama.
- Yes, sir!

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.140
Where's Petty Officer Fa?!

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.710
Sorry I'm late.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.270
What difference is she going to make?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:46.050
You fully understand, right?!

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.780
You are not to go out unless
ordered by the captain or myself.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.490
Our present priority
is to retrieve the shuttle!

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.360
I understand.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.270
The last thing I want is to have to be
"corrected" by Lieutenant Quattro.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.440
<i>Mobile suit team! Prepare to take off!</i>

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.270
<i>Look out for enemies from all directions!</i>

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:08.610
Two battleships detected!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.980
Believed to be the Argama
and the Radish!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.310
Hurry and confirm it!

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:15.120
What?! Yazan's team has left!

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.950
What?!

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.660
If I were worrying about the red tape...

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.160
...I'd lag behind my own allies!

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.300
Hey! Will you two keep it down?!

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.010
If you don't behave yourselves,
I'm not taking you to space with me!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:48.980
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.650
Helping people is great, but you can only
sacrifice so much of yourself.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.160
Of course.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:57.590
I just feel I need to take care of
someone in place of Commodore Blex.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.290
Oh, and be sure to wait for
the right moment...

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.300
...to inform the A.E.U.G.
of the Commodore's death.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.700
For sure.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.240
Those in space already know
about your return.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.500
There's nothing to worry about
with Captain Bright.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.040
Thank you, Hayato.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.170
I've ended up having to rely on you again.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.210
Don't mention it.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.340
Ever since that colony
was dropped on the Moon...

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:21.220
...the Colonies and the cities
there have been terrified.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.590
I hear it's pressured some into considering
an alliance with the Titans.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:27.780
I'm aware of it.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.000
However, there are
an increasing number of people...

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.090
...who hate the Titans
for dropping the colony.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.600
That's right. That's why...!

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.000
Now that Commodore Blex Forer
has passed away...

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.050
...you, Lieutenant Quattro Bajeena
must take control of the A.E.U.G..

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.220
I have another favor to ask you.

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.320
It's from Captain Bright's wife.

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.620
Yes.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:59.720
That lady's always on top of things -
Mrs. Mirai Yashima.

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:02.350
Have a safe trip.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.420
<i>We will reach critical point in one minute.</i>

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.260
<i>May I ask that all passengers</i>
<i>check that their seatbelts are fastened.</i>

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.570
<i>Now then, have an enjoyable journey.</i>

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:16.030
Karaba, the A.E.U.G., and also the Axis.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.610
It's a tremendous burden
I'm suddenly handed.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:23.280
Five...four...three...two...one!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.270
Enemy mobile suits detected!
They're heading straight toward us!

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.770
They've come sooner than I expected.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.670
We'll proceed with our plan!

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.110
We'll retrieve the shuttle
even if we sacrifice the Argama to do it!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:51.770
Earth's...!

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.330
Stay alert for any missiles
from the Earth!

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.610
That'll do.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.460
Send out the mobile suit team!

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:21.300
Mega-particle cannon,
lock on to the enemy fleet!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.480
Don't forget, the Radish is to act
as a shield for the Argama!

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.640
Emma! Taking off!

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:40.950
You guys, go after the Nemos!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:41.990
<i>Roger!</i>

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.450
You can run, but you can't hide!

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.730
Good, he's coming after me.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.550
Can't we see the Argama yet?

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:13.490
I'm sure they were told
that we'd be up to this line.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.290
But rather than waiting here
for them to contact us...

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.350
...we'd better go
directly to Sweetwater.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.560
There's no way we can do that!

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.060
We'll be there in a week
on inertia flight!

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.330
That won't do.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.490
I have a schedule to keep.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.760
B-But!

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:27.860
I'm well aware of the dangers of
remaining like this.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:30.610
Could you lend me a boat?

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.140
You're leaving on a boat?!

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.910
That's crazy! First of all,
they'll never find you...!

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.710
It'll be all right.
It's the Argama we're talking about.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.990
The mobile suit team is moving away.

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.990
We're not at our rendezvous point yet!

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.050
Have our mobile suits standby!

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:56.960
What are our damages?!

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:58.560
No air leaks!

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:01.160
Yazan's team is presently overpowering
the enemy mobile suits!

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.430
What about Jerid's team?!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:04.830
I've left Lieutenant Jerid in charge!

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.110
What's going on with the Argama?!

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.480
Nothing. Their mobile suit team
hasn't launched yet, either!

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.510
Why...?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.120
You guys just won't give up, will you?!

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.900
The Nemos are suffering slight damage!
Unable to fight!

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.940
If we wait any longer, it will be
impossible to make contact with the shuttle.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.610
Okay! Full speed ahead!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.770
Also send out the mobile suits!

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:39.940
Rick Dias team, taking off!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:42.950
Methuss, taking off!

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.610
Zeta Gundam, let's do it!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.590
The Argama's making a move!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.630
I guess their guest is up here!

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.420
Prepare for anti-air battle!

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.930
- Jerid's team is ready to take off!
- Good!

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.610
The Launcher can only be fired once.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:19.480
After that, your Hizacks
will be left immobile.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.750
I'm sorry to seem selfish...

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:24.290
...but I find this machine
the easiest to operate.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:27.150
If you feel better that way, that's fine.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.680
Once we lure them in,
I'll fire two signal flares.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.090
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.190
Later, Mouar.

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:35.500
Later, Jerid.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.660
- <i>Methuss, go to back up Emma's team!</i>
- Roger!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.340
A Gabthley?

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:50.780
- <i>Leave it to Kamille!</i>
- Right!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.380
A damaged Hizack?!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.720
<i>Don't fall behind, Fa!</i>

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.700
Where's Zeta Gundam?!

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.330
There!

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.370
What was that?!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.710
What?!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:29.010
You're finished, Mk. II!

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.350
- <i>Squadron Leader Yazan!</i>
- Yeah?!

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:33.050
- <i>Please go after the Argama at once!</i>
- What?!

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:41.060
<i>The Zeta Gundam's also launched.</i>
<i>Lieutenant Jerid is presently battling it!</i>

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.130
Can't he leave it to me?!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.930
Oh, no! He's headed for the Argama!

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:51.270
- <i>Lieutenant Emma!</i>
- Katz?!

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:59.080
- Why'd you come?!
- <i>Didn't you feel anything, Lieutenant?!</i>

00:16:59.250 --> 00:16:59.740
Roger!

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.390
- Any contact with the shuttle?
- Not yet, sir.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.790
The Radish's defensive line
behind us is collapsing.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.230
- Don't slow down!
- But, unless we do...!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:15.730
We'll endure this until the final moment!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.000
Shuttle in sight!
They're increasing altitude!

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.740
- The boat's leaving the shuttle!
- <i>I wish you luck!</i>

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.440
He's got to be insane!

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:29.480
We'll descend now!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.780
- A core boat has left the shuttle.
- That's it! Retrieve it!

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:36.920
I'll do my best!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.980
That's not good enough!
Make sure you retrieve it!

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:46.320
Stop!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.970
What must I do to stop the Zeta?!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.310
Stop! Zeta!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.990
<i>Someone's watching!</i>

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:17.320
<i>Who is it?!</i>

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.100
Got you!

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:22.630
Not so fast!

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.810
Move, Jerid!
I'll defeat the Zeta Gundam myself!

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.170
Yazan!

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.140
He's stopped!

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:39.980
Sarah, now!

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:41.150
Y-Yes!

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:44.990
Kamille!

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.130
Again...!

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:55.060
Don't fire!!

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:56.990
What?!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.760
Fire, Sarah!

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.030
Y-Yes!

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:04.580
We're not going to make it!

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:05.610
Sarah?!

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:19.890
What?!

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:28.560
It vanished...!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:32.330
The shuttle vanished?!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.370
Captain.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:35.800
Lieutenant Quattro's boat
is arriving on board!

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.790
Call back the mobile suit team.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:55.330
- We'll reorganize the fleet!
- Yes, sir!

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.660
The Argama's likely reached
the other side of Earth by now.

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:08.570
Almost, Jerid.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.570
Yeah.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:13.130
But that Launcher really works.
It's going to come in useful.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:15.770
If you and Sarah will assist me
with it again, that is.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.310
<i>Jerid, what about...?</i>

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.440
I know.
I feel it about Sarah as well.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.250
Katz.
And Kamille.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.130
Good job, Kamille.

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:31.930
Fa!

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:35.630
Hey, Fa!

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:37.740
I was wrong about earlier.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:40.260
I know that!

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.310
Fa.

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.310
This isn't the time
to be quarreling with each other.

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:52.920
In our situation,
we could be killed any day.

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:55.450
I'm sure I've got my faults.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:58.960
And I'll apologize for them
as much as you wish.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:02.120
But you're being somewhat
immature yourself.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.990
We're no longer little children.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.830
I know that, Kamille.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:14.600
Bye!

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:17.210
Hey!

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:19.870
What's wrong with him?

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.110
You've gone through much hardship, Captain.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:23.810
- I see an increase in gray hairs.
- Really?!

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:27.320
You've noticed yourself, haven't you?

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:31.220
W-Well, it seems that I'm not suited to be
a father figure for Kamille and the others.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.460
Kamille doesn't need a father figure
any longer.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.220
This is from your true children.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.860
Th-Thank you.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.060
Nothing could make me happier.

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:45.270
- Later.
- Bye.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.850
<i>Daddy, I'm good!</i>

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:01.550
<i>I can now do all my spelling homework.</i>

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:05.420
<i>Look. I got a hundred!</i>
<i>Great, huh?!</i>

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:08.460
<i>Did you know Mommy's worried</i>
<i>that she's getting fat?</i>

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:10.760
<i>My turn, Daddy, can you hear me?</i>

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:13.030
<i>I'm running everyday!</i>

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.630
<i>I'll protect Cheimin and Mommy...</i>

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:19.130
<i>...so don't worry, and go get</i>
<i>those bad guys, Daddy!</i>

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:22.140
<i>Mommy always talks to us about you</i>
<i>before bedtime...</i>

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:26.470
<i>...that you're on this big, big ship,</i>
<i>and you're using Gundams!</i>

00:22:26.550 --> 00:22:28.880
<i>When you come home...!</i>

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.540
Seeing the Jupitris and its
unpredictable movements...

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:50.440
...the Argama decides to scout the vessel.

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:53.140
Reccoa Londe is handed the task.

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:57.170
Amidst this, Kamille senses
a dangerous scent coming from Reccoa.

00:23:57.550 --> 00:24:01.510
And while on the Jupitris,
Reccoa meets Scirocco.

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:07.360
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Jupitris Infiltration".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
The Jupitris Infiltration

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:10.560
You will see the tears of time.
